From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:56:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: ath11k: limit scan channel list messages to 2048
 bytes

On the Zyxel NWA220AX-6E the QCN9074 serves both 5 GHz and 6 GHz. With
a country that allows the full 6 GHz band, such as US or the default
00, its channel list grows to 85 channels and ath11k sends it as one
2400 byte WMI message. The firmware accepts it, but the next vdev start
times out and no AP comes up on that radio, on 5 GHz or 6 GHz:

  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: failed to vdev 0 create peer for AP: -110
  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: Timeout in receiving vdev delete response

Countries that limit 6 GHz to UNII-5 (TW, DE) stay at 49 channels and
were not affected, nor is a 6 GHz-only radio (60 channels).

Add a patch that keeps each scan channel list message within 2048
bytes (72 channels). Longer lists use the existing append flag.

Tested on the Zyxel NWA220AX-6E with country US: 5 GHz channel 36 HE80
and 6 GHz channels 37 and 197 HE80 come up, with the list sent as
72 + 13 channels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
---
 ...-channel-list-messages-to-2048-bytes.patch | 56 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/953-wifi-ath11k-limit-scan-channel-list-messages-to-2048-bytes.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/953-wifi-ath11k-limit-scan-channel-list-messages-to-2048-bytes.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/953-wifi-ath11k-limit-scan-channel-list-messages-to-2048-bytes.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..9e3b203047
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/953-wifi-ath11k-limit-scan-channel-list-messages-to-2048-bytes.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+From: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: limit scan channel list messages to 2048 bytes
+
+ath11k sends the channel list in as few WMI_SCAN_CHAN_LIST_CMDID
+messages as the WMI endpoint's max_msg_len allows, and marks the
+following ones with WMI_APPEND_TO_EXISTING_CHAN_LIST_FLAG.
+
+QCN9074 firmware 0x290b8862 (target credit size 4096) does not handle a
+list larger than about 2 KB in one message. On a QCN9074 that covers
+5 GHz and 6 GHz, a country with the full 6 GHz band (for example US)
+gives 85 channels, sent as one 2400 byte message. The firmware accepts
+it, but the next vdev start never completes and the AP fails to come
+up on any band:
+
+  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: failed to vdev 0 create peer for AP: -110
+  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: Timeout in receiving vdev delete response
+
+Lists of up to 72 channels (2036 bytes) work. Keep every message
+within 2048 bytes, so the 85 channels go out as 72 + 13 with the append
+flag. Lists that fit in one message are sent as before.
+
+Signed-off-by: Mark Chiou <chiouss@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+@@ -2552,6 +2552,12 @@ int ath11k_wmi_send_scan_stop_cmd(struct
+ 	return ret;
+ }
+ 
++/*
++ * QCN9074 firmware hangs on a scan channel list larger than this, although it
++ * accepts bigger WMI messages. Longer lists are sent in several messages.
++ */
++#define ATH11K_WMI_SCAN_CHAN_LIST_MAX_LEN	2048
++
+ int ath11k_wmi_send_scan_chan_list_cmd(struct ath11k *ar,
+ 				       struct scan_chan_list_params *chan_list)
+ {
+@@ -2564,13 +2570,14 @@ int ath11k_wmi_send_scan_chan_list_cmd(s
+ 	void *ptr;
+ 	int i, ret, len;
+ 	u16 num_send_chans, num_sends = 0, max_chan_limit = 0;
+-	u32 *reg1, *reg2;
++	u32 *reg1, *reg2, max_msg_len;
+ 
+ 	tchan_info = chan_list->ch_param;
+ 	while (chan_list->nallchans) {
+ 		len = sizeof(*cmd) + TLV_HDR_SIZE;
+-		max_chan_limit = (wmi->wmi_ab->max_msg_len[ar->pdev_idx] - len) /
+-			sizeof(*chan_info);
++		max_msg_len = min_t(u32, wmi->wmi_ab->max_msg_len[ar->pdev_idx],
++				    ATH11K_WMI_SCAN_CHAN_LIST_MAX_LEN);
++		max_chan_limit = (max_msg_len - len) / sizeof(*chan_info);
+ 
+ 		if (chan_list->nallchans > max_chan_limit)
+ 			num_send_chans = max_chan_limit;
